1. PROBLEM STATEMENT:
The Flight Booking System is a C++ application developed using a Singly Linked List to manage flight booking records. 
It allows users to book flights, display all bookings, search for a booking using Booking ID, and cancel bookings.
It also demonstrates dynamic memory allocation functions such as malloc(), calloc(), realloc(), and free().

2. Objectives

To implement a Singly Linked List in C++.
To insert and display flight booking records.
To search for bookings using Booking ID.
To cancel bookings by deleting the required node.
To understand dynamic memory allocation and deallocation.
To learn linked-list traversal and pointer operations.

3. Algorithm

Start the program.
Initialize head = NULL.
Display the menu and accept the user's choice.
Create a node and insert flight details to book a flight.
Display all bookings by traversing the linked list.
Search for a booking using its Booking ID.
Cancel a booking by updating links and deleting the node.
Demonstrate malloc(), calloc(), realloc(), and free().
Repeat the menu until the user selects Exit.
Release all remaining nodes and stop the program.
